[TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router6
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Router6’s Linux firewall (iptables) in the forwarding path. The FORWARD chain has blanket drop rules that block all traffic arriving from the uplink.

Mechanism: Traffic from other groups reaches router6 via its uplink interface eth2 (to router3). Router6’s iptables contains:
- A very narrow allow: FORWARD -s 172.16.10.0/24 -d 172.18.51.1 tcp dport 80
- Then FORWARD -i eth2 -p tcp DROP; FORWARD -i eth2 -p udp DROP; FORWARD -i eth2 DROP
As a result, any forwarded flows entering router6 on eth2 (including ICMP, most TCP/UDP) are dropped. Traffic that originates within 172.18.50.0/24 and 172.18.51.0/24 does not hit -i eth2 and thus works fine inside that “other group.”

Localization: Router6, interf
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=38
